---

Hypertensive urgency = severe HT (SBP > 180 or DBP > 120) WITHOUT acute end-organ damage. Hypertensive emergency = same BP + end-organ damage (acute kidney injury, encephalopathy, retinopathy with papilledema, ACS, pulmonary edema, aortic dissection, eclampsia, intracranial bleed). ACC/AHA 2017 + JNC HT guideline: (1) Urgency: oral antihypertensive, gradual lowering over hours-days, target < 160/100 then to goal over weeks; outpatient management. (2) Avoid sublingual nifedipine (uncontrolled rapid drop → ischemic stroke/MI). (3) IV agents only for true emergency. (4) Address adherence, identify white-coat, secondary HT (Conn, pheo, OSA, renovascular). (5) Resume home regimen + reassess; outpatient follow-up.', NULL,
